# review.md, review-change.md and review-issue.md say what the enrollment review and the change review check, and what
# the draft reply to an issue says (.github/workflows/build.yaml reads main's copies), and
# .claude/skills/write-to-maintainer/ says how every message to a maintainer is written and checked.
#
# The other lines own each file that changes what a workflow runs or what a verdict is, whoever opens the pull request:
#   /.github/                     the workflows and the scripts they run.
#   /src/                         the oss_verify package: `oss-verify check` and `oss-verify validate`.
#   /infra/                       the toolchains `oss-verify check` builds with (infra/toolchains.tsv,
#                                 infra/base-builder/), and the code it runs in build containers (infra/checks/).
#   /seeds/                       the seeded projects, which `oss-verify check` builds as it builds projects/.
#   .claude/, CLAUDE*.md,         what Claude Code loads in the review job, which holds an identity token: settings
#   AGENTS*.md (at any depth),    and hooks, skills, instructions and MCP servers.
#   /.mcp.json
#   /*.py, /pyproject.toml,       what python3 and pytest load from the top of the checkout, and the Python and
#   /uv.lock, /.python-version    dependency versions that `uv run oss-verify` installs. Each python3 -c and -m of
#   and pytest's configuration    the workflows runs with -P, so no new directory at the top shadows a module, and
#   files                         tests.yaml runs pytest with -c pyproject.toml, so it reads no other configuration
#                                 file.
# A pull request from a fork that changes no file under projects/ passes the enrollment checks, and tests.yaml runs the
# fork's own copy of itself, so these lines are what keeps such a change from merging on one person's reading.
#
# The ruleset of main requires a code owner's approval, so a change to any of these files, or to this file, which says
# who owns them, needs the approval of a member of @theorem-labs/engineering, a team of people. No other file has an
# owner, so no other pull request needs a code owner: a change to tests/, docs/ or one projects/<name>/ needs none.
# These lines stay the last patterns of the file: the last pattern that matches a file decides its owner.
/.github/ @theorem-labs/engineering
/src/ @theorem-labs/engineering
/infra/ @theorem-labs/engineering
/seeds/ @theorem-labs/engineering
.claude/ @theorem-labs/engineering
CLAUDE*.md @theorem-labs/engineering
AGENTS*.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/.mcp.json @theorem-labs/engineering
/*.py @theorem-labs/engineering
/pytest.ini @theorem-labs/engineering
/.pytest.ini @theorem-labs/engineering
/pyproject.toml @theorem-labs/engineering
/uv.lock @theorem-labs/engineering
/.python-version @theorem-labs/engineering
/setup.cfg @theorem-labs/engineering
/tox.ini @theorem-labs/engineering
/review.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/review-change.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/review-issue.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/.claude/skills/write-to-maintainer/ @theorem-labs/engineering
/.github/CODEOWNERS @theorem-labs/engineering
